1
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:06,401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

2
00:00:06,411 --> 00:00:08,400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

3
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:09,950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

5
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

6
00:00:12,899 --> 00:00:13,900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

7
00:00:13,911 --> 00:00:14,912
[or any particular group of people.]

8
00:00:14,976 --> 00:00:18,840
We've already issued an invitation to bid through e-bidding.

9
00:00:19,083 --> 00:00:21,600
We haven't made the terms of reference too restrictive,

10
00:00:21,627 --> 00:00:24,840
because we want to give young entrepreneurs and smaller companies

11
00:00:24,901 --> 00:00:26,702
a chance to submit their bids too.

12
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,520
Why don't we bid on her Smart Card project?

13
00:00:28,751 --> 00:00:30,752
Government contracts require deep pockets

14
00:00:30,856 --> 00:00:31,857
because payments take forever.

15
00:00:32,011 --> 00:00:35,120
A small company like ours doesn't stand a chance.

16
00:00:35,243 --> 00:00:36,560
I'm here to see the Minister.

17
00:00:36,700 --> 00:00:39,720
I've agreed to take the money and stay away from the Director.

18
00:00:39,744 --> 00:00:40,745
Ten million.

19
00:00:40,795 --> 00:00:42,170
And how can I be sure

20
00:00:43,526 --> 00:00:44,960
that once you get the money,

21
00:00:45,792 --> 00:00:47,400
you'll really leave my husband alone?

22
00:00:47,483 --> 00:00:48,840
I'm a woman of my word.

23
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:51,480
Have you talked to Ta lately?

24
00:00:51,494 --> 00:00:53,040
Why do you ask, Uncle Phop?

25
00:00:53,259 --> 00:00:56,590
She suddenly blocked me on everything.

26
00:00:56,608 --> 00:00:58,880
She didn't even tell me why. I don't know what's wrong.

27
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:01,480
Ma'am, that bitch Mutta sent you a package.

28
00:01:01,627 --> 00:01:03,220
- What is that?
- It's money.

29
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:04,480
There must be millions in here.

30
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:08,101
Our informant just sent us these photos. This just happened.

31
00:01:08,736 --> 00:01:09,920
Mutta! You bitch!

32
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:14,880
[Foster Home]

33
00:01:16,774 --> 00:01:17,775
What are your names, dears?

34
00:01:20,865 --> 00:01:22,800
Answer when an adult asks you a question.

35
00:01:24,226 --> 00:01:27,160
I'm Munin. This is Mutta.

36
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:29,851
"Yes, ma'am."

37
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:34,576
When an adult asks you something, you must answer politely.

38
00:01:34,747 --> 00:01:36,760
Always say "yes, ma'am" or "yes, sir." Understand?

39
00:01:37,334 --> 00:01:38,335
Yes, ma'am.

40
00:01:39,700 --> 00:01:42,520
From now on, you two will start a new life here.

41
00:01:43,142 --> 00:01:45,880
You'll make new friends and follow new rules.

42
00:01:46,646 --> 00:01:50,160
And I'll be your new mother here.

43
00:01:52,374 --> 00:01:54,175
What about our mother?

44
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,600
Will she come here too... ma'am?

45
00:01:58,576 --> 00:01:59,577
No, dear.

46
00:02:00,331 --> 00:02:01,332
You don't have to worry about that.

47
00:02:01,558 --> 00:02:05,440
She'll never be able to hurt you again.

48
00:02:07,771 --> 00:02:10,920
Take the two girls to bathe and get changed.

49
00:02:10,997 --> 00:02:13,000
Then show them where they'll be sleeping.

50
00:02:21,046 --> 00:02:24,360
Mutta, we won't have to see Mom again. Aren't you happy?

51
00:02:24,798 --> 00:02:25,799
Yeah.

52
00:02:27,915 --> 00:02:31,000
When will the twins' mother be released?

53
00:02:32,992 --> 00:02:34,700
The court sentenced her to life in prison.

54
00:03:57,014 --> 00:03:58,015
Mutta,

55
00:03:58,150 --> 00:04:01,120
if you're around, please guide me.

56
00:04:01,744 --> 00:04:02,891
Help me make the right choice.

57
00:04:03,654 --> 00:04:04,680
I can't afford to get this wrong.

58
00:04:10,408 --> 00:04:11,800
I'm betting ten million on one go.

59
00:04:12,424 --> 00:04:14,640
If I win, I'll get a hundred million back.

60
00:04:14,883 --> 00:04:17,180
But if I lose, I'll lose everything.

61
00:04:18,918 --> 00:04:20,440
Will I finally get my revenge?

62
00:04:21,072 --> 00:04:22,760
It all comes down to this one click.

63
00:04:42,771 --> 00:04:44,568
Why are you calling? To make up with me?

64
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:46,350
I'm busy. Bye.

65
00:04:46,563 --> 00:04:47,960
I'm not calling to make up.

66
00:04:48,606 --> 00:04:51,700
I just wanted to ask if you've broken up with Uncle Phop.

67
00:04:52,728 --> 00:04:54,947
Why? Happy to hear that?

68
00:04:55,822 --> 00:04:58,600
If it's true, of course I am. I can keep pursuing you.

69
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:00,801
Veekit,

70
00:05:01,182 --> 00:05:03,680
you need to stop trying to claim me after your uncle.

71
00:05:04,216 --> 00:05:05,440
I've told you before, haven't I?

72
00:05:05,651 --> 00:05:07,960
I'm not the same sweet, innocent Mutta anymore.

73
00:05:08,419 --> 00:05:09,800
That's exactly why

74
00:05:10,680 --> 00:05:12,250
I like you even more now.

75
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:23,224
It's rare to see Phop staying home for once.

76
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:25,720
Normally, on holidays like this,

77
00:05:26,046 --> 00:05:28,590
he'd be traveling somewhere, either here or abroad.

78
00:05:29,251 --> 00:05:30,640
I wonder what's gotten into him.

79
00:05:35,900 --> 00:05:37,280
- Na.
- Yes?

80
00:05:37,379 --> 00:05:38,800
Go cleaning up outside for now.

81
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,001
Yes, ma'am.

82
00:05:46,984 --> 00:05:48,720
I bought him back with money.

83
00:05:49,176 --> 00:05:51,520
If I'd known it was this easy, I'd have done it ages ago.

84
00:05:54,222 --> 00:05:55,440
You bought him back?

85
00:05:56,088 --> 00:05:57,700
What do you mean? From whom?

86
00:05:59,702 --> 00:06:02,080
I bought Phop back from that Mutta.

87
00:06:03,584 --> 00:06:06,160
I offered her a sum of money

88
00:06:06,262 --> 00:06:07,640
to stay away from Phop.

89
00:06:07,851 --> 00:06:11,240
At first, I thought I might just be throwing my money away.

90
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:15,240
But believe it or not, even that whore has some decency.

91
00:06:15,414 --> 00:06:17,160
She actually agreed to leave him, Soi!

92
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:18,921
Really?

93
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:23,120
Thank goodness! Who knew it would be this easy?

94
00:06:23,587 --> 00:06:25,121
So how much did you pay that bitch?

95
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,681
Ten million.

96
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:28,280
Ten million?

97
00:06:30,736 --> 00:06:34,971
No wonder she agreed. I'd take the money too.

98
00:06:35,398 --> 00:06:37,760
Ten million in exchange for one useless man?

99
00:06:38,056 --> 00:06:39,720
Who'd be stupid enough to choose the man?

100
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:46,680
But it was worth it to get your husband back.

101
00:06:46,914 --> 00:06:49,134
Your children have their father back, too.

102
00:06:49,342 --> 00:06:52,760
And your family is whole and happy again.

103
00:06:53,203 --> 00:06:56,792
Even twenty million would be a bargain, if you ask me.

104
00:07:02,275 --> 00:07:03,276
Hello?

105
00:07:03,624 --> 00:07:05,280
Have you seen the money I transferred?

106
00:07:05,795 --> 00:07:08,440
Yeah, I have. Why the hell did you send me fifty million?

107
00:07:09,142 --> 00:07:12,200
Didn't you say we needed deep pockets to get into government contracts?

108
00:07:12,630 --> 00:07:15,800
We're going to land the smart card project from the ministry.

109
00:07:16,267 --> 00:07:17,680
You can get started today.

110
00:07:18,171 --> 00:07:20,172
Where did you get all that money?

111
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,021
Crypto trading.

112
00:07:23,464 --> 00:07:24,465
I've got to go.

113
00:07:29,200 --> 00:07:30,201
Director.

114
00:07:31,011 --> 00:07:33,358
Mutta, what kind of game are you playing with me now?

115
00:07:33,779 --> 00:07:36,280
One minute you're gone, the next you're back. I'm so confused.

116
00:07:37,219 --> 00:07:40,400
Keeping you guessing makes our love life more exciting.

117
00:07:41,220 --> 00:07:42,521
Let's have lunch together today.

118
00:07:54,723 --> 00:07:58,300
It's the latest iPhone. That's my phone.

119
00:07:58,643 --> 00:08:01,280
She broke her promise after all. That bitch!

120
00:08:03,502 --> 00:08:06,050
I don't have an appointment. May I still see him?

121
00:08:06,824 --> 00:08:08,974
Mutta, what the hell are you playing at?

122
00:08:09,494 --> 00:08:10,731
Ten million!

123
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:14,960
A low-ranking civil servant like you couldn't earn that much in three lifetimes!

124
00:08:15,104 --> 00:08:16,520
Instead of holding on to it for dear life.

125
00:08:16,566 --> 00:08:17,700
What kind of game are you playing with me?

126
00:08:17,968 --> 00:08:19,520
I'm just following your advice, ma'am.

127
00:08:20,064 --> 00:08:23,090
You said smart people these days trade crypto.

128
00:08:23,296 --> 00:08:24,680
So I thought I'd give it a try.

129
00:08:24,992 --> 00:08:27,760
As luck would have it, I made a little profit.

130
00:08:27,926 --> 00:08:31,250
Enough to get by, so I thought I'd return your ten million.

131
00:08:31,550 --> 00:08:34,640
Thank you so much for showing me how to get rich.

132
00:08:34,968 --> 00:08:36,680
And for giving me the money to get started.

133
00:08:37,539 --> 00:08:38,540
I'm forever grateful.

134
00:08:40,043 --> 00:08:41,044
You bitch!

135
00:08:41,115 --> 00:08:42,240
Get out!

136
00:08:42,406 --> 00:08:44,200
- Get out!
- Calm down, ma'am. Get a hold of yourself.

137
00:08:44,486 --> 00:08:45,487
Please calm down.

138
00:08:48,054 --> 00:08:49,320
Good for you, now that you're rich.

139
00:08:50,222 --> 00:08:51,640
So you'll leave my husband alone, right?

140
00:08:52,392 --> 00:08:55,120
Just so you know, Phop isn't rolling in money.

141
00:08:55,278 --> 00:08:56,400
It's all my money!

142
00:08:58,126 --> 00:08:59,400
Let me make one thing clear, ma'am.

143
00:09:00,547 --> 00:09:03,560
I'm not seeing the Director for his money.

144
00:09:03,950 --> 00:09:05,760
It's purely for the amazing sex.

145
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:07,700
I've got a thing for a man like him.

146
00:09:08,147 --> 00:09:10,800
Why not share something this good?

147
00:09:11,235 --> 00:09:14,760
Once I'm done with him, I send him home for you to enjoy.

148
00:09:15,356 --> 00:09:17,157
It's not like he's going to wear out on me.

149
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:19,301
Mutta, you bitch!

150
00:09:19,891 --> 00:09:22,720
I'll kill you!

151
00:09:27,987 --> 00:09:29,080
As if you haven't tried before.

152
00:09:30,291 --> 00:09:32,520
Too bad for you, I'm not that easy to kill.

153
00:09:32,862 --> 00:09:34,880
You made a huge mistake

154
00:09:35,187 --> 00:09:36,800
letting me live this long.

155
00:09:39,790 --> 00:09:42,600
What the hell are you talking about? When did I ever try to kill you?

156
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:45,441
Do you have any proof?

157
00:09:45,827 --> 00:09:47,600
- Should we get you drug-tested?
- Go ahead.

158
00:09:48,126 --> 00:09:51,160
But you might find traces of the Director's bodily fluids, too.

159
00:09:51,619 --> 00:09:53,080
We just finished having sex.

160
00:09:54,872 --> 00:09:55,773
You bitch!

161
00:09:55,779 --> 00:09:57,220
Please calm down, ma'am.

162
00:09:57,223 --> 00:09:58,660
- Let go of me!
- Ma'am!

163
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:00,601
Mutta, you bitch!

164
00:10:02,480 --> 00:10:05,400
Get this through your thick skull.

165
00:10:06,363 --> 00:10:07,960
As long as I'm alive,

166
00:10:08,608 --> 00:10:10,680
I'll devote every ounce of my energy

167
00:10:11,206 --> 00:10:12,720
to messing with your head.

168
00:10:13,579 --> 00:10:14,920
You won't get away from me.

169
00:10:15,995 --> 00:10:17,000
Mutta, you bitch!

170
00:10:17,195 --> 00:10:18,680
Mutta!

171
00:10:18,688 --> 00:10:20,200
Let go of me! I'll kill her!

172
00:10:20,240 --> 00:10:21,680
- I'll kill her!
- Ma'am, please!

173
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:23,720
- That bitch Mutta!
- You can't, ma'am!

174
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:26,640
The election is coming up. You can't kill anyone now!

175
00:10:26,736 --> 00:10:28,400
What's one more person?

176
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,800
- Please calm down, ma'am!
- Let go of me!

177
00:10:32,166 --> 00:10:33,167
Please sit down.

178
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:34,468
Calm down, ma'am.

179
00:10:38,448 --> 00:10:40,480
Every political party is looking for a way to bring you down.

180
00:10:41,376 --> 00:10:42,480
Please be patient a little longer, ma'am.

181
00:10:43,243 --> 00:10:44,760
Once the election is over and your party forms the government,

182
00:10:45,147 --> 00:10:46,500
we can deal with her then.

183
00:10:57,654 --> 00:10:58,655
Jolene.

184
00:11:02,131 --> 00:11:03,132
What are you all doing?

185
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:07,280
We just submitted our bid for the smart card project.

186
00:11:09,851 --> 00:11:11,560
Please let us win.

187
00:11:13,275 --> 00:11:15,880
Oh, Munin! Perfect timing. Come pray with us.

188
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,320
Everyone else has already prayed. Come on.

189
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:19,201
Let's go pray at the spirit house.

190
00:11:19,643 --> 00:11:21,440
Come on, hurry.

191
00:11:27,726 --> 00:11:29,955
Hey, take this seriously.

192
00:11:30,200 --> 00:11:32,120
If we win this contract,

193
00:11:32,254 --> 00:11:34,446
we'll be able to use it to pitch for other projects

194
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:36,300
and walk in with our heads held high.

195
00:11:36,451 --> 00:11:37,452
Let me show you.

196
00:11:40,163 --> 00:11:43,640
Hello, I'm Jolene from Queen Byte,

197
00:11:43,774 --> 00:11:48,720
the company behind the smart card system used by over 70 million Thais.

198
00:11:50,275 --> 00:11:52,000
I'd love to get the credit,

199
00:11:52,627 --> 00:11:54,080
but what I want even more

200
00:11:54,995 --> 00:11:57,450
is to wreak havoc on that bitch Nopnapha's career.

201
00:11:57,952 --> 00:11:59,800
Just wait and see.

202
00:12:00,918 --> 00:12:02,600
I'll make her suffer like never before.

203
00:12:09,990 --> 00:12:11,400
It's from Mr.  Thanong, ma'am.

204
00:12:12,811 --> 00:12:14,560
Deposit it in the Singapore bank as usual.

205
00:12:14,832 --> 00:12:16,520
But use a different account from last time.

206
00:12:17,078 --> 00:12:18,079
Yes, ma'am.

207
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:29,718
Touch, I've gone through all the company profiles.

208
00:12:30,395 --> 00:12:32,360
Which company do you think looks the most promising?

209
00:12:32,728 --> 00:12:34,680
There are three or four promising companies.

210
00:12:35,240 --> 00:12:36,376
I've shortlisted them for you.

211
00:12:36,600 --> 00:12:39,601
One company's partner works in the US.

212
00:12:39,998 --> 00:12:41,400
They might have some new software

213
00:12:41,656 --> 00:12:42,960
that we could use, too.

214
00:12:43,307 --> 00:12:46,240
Yeah, I'm interested in that company as well.

215
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:50,921
Just a second.

216
00:12:51,110 --> 00:12:53,758
Go play somewhere else. Mommy's busy.

217
00:12:53,886 --> 00:12:57,240
Mom, you forgot to tell Oshi to buy me the Bambinana Red Hat!

218
00:12:57,672 --> 00:12:59,040
Wait, what did you say?

219
00:12:59,534 --> 00:13:02,974
Bambinana! Bambinana!

220
00:13:03,478 --> 00:13:06,060
- Oshi!
- Yes?

221
00:13:06,115 --> 00:13:07,520
- Come here for a second.
- Yes, ma'am.

222
00:13:08,083 --> 00:13:11,520
What on earth is this Bamba-baba, Bibi-baba thing?

223
00:13:11,582 --> 00:13:13,520
Oh, it's an art toy, ma'am.

224
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:16,440
It's what Titus asked you to get for her birthday.

225
00:13:18,043 --> 00:13:19,100
I must've forgotten.

226
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:20,806
Go get one for her. How much does it cost?

227
00:13:20,821 --> 00:13:24,020
Oh, it's sold out, ma'am. It's a limited edition.

228
00:13:24,040 --> 00:13:26,300
It went on sale this morning, and fewer than a hundred were available.

229
00:13:26,726 --> 00:13:29,000
I've tried asking people who managed to buy one,

230
00:13:29,027 --> 00:13:30,800
but nobody's willing to resell theirs, ma'am.

231
00:13:31,862 --> 00:13:35,600
Titus, I'll buy you one when the next version comes out, okay?

232
00:13:35,620 --> 00:13:36,960
I promise I won't forget this time.

233
00:13:37,342 --> 00:13:40,131
- No! I want this one!
- Titus!

234
00:13:40,227 --> 00:13:43,400
It's wearing a red hat! A red hat!

235
00:13:43,915 --> 00:13:46,656
- I want this one! I want this one!
- Phop, come here!

236
00:13:46,784 --> 00:13:49,150
Hurry! Your son's throwing a tantrum!

237
00:13:49,211 --> 00:13:50,212
What's wrong?

238
00:13:50,312 --> 00:13:53,313
- It's got a red hat, Mom! I want this one!
- What a headache!

239
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,240
- Titus, sweetheart! Titus!
- Wait, where were we?

240
00:13:55,250 --> 00:13:56,520
- What does Daddy's precious little girl want?
- Go on.

241
00:13:56,982 --> 00:13:57,983
Okay.

242
00:13:58,144 --> 00:13:59,400
And don't forget, for this project,

243
00:13:59,450 --> 00:14:01,720
- We're only taking 15%.
- What do you want?

244
00:14:01,899 --> 00:14:04,040
I want Bambinana!

245
00:14:04,120 --> 00:14:06,550
Hey, get down first! You'll hurt yourself!

246
00:14:06,800 --> 00:14:07,801
What do you want, sweetheart?

247
00:14:07,811 --> 00:14:10,812
I want the Bambinana Red Hat!

248
00:14:10,840 --> 00:14:12,720
The one wearing a red hat!

249
00:14:12,800 --> 00:14:15,301
Oh, how about Toi Red Hat instead, sweetie?

250
00:14:15,891 --> 00:14:17,400
Dad, what are you talking about?

251
00:14:20,456 --> 00:14:22,320
Excuse me, sir. That's a singer.

252
00:14:23,457 --> 00:14:24,458
I know that!

253
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,520
Here you go, Mutta.

254
00:14:41,502 --> 00:14:44,680
What should we have for lunch? I'm sick of cafeteria food.

255
00:14:44,819 --> 00:14:46,720
How about Som Tam Je Pu outside the Ministry?

256
00:14:48,019 --> 00:14:50,120
Oh, let's go! Come on, get up!

257
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,201
It's not even noon yet.

258
00:14:54,611 --> 00:14:56,360
If we wait until noon, we won't get to eat.

259
00:14:57,086 --> 00:14:58,840
You know how crowded that place gets.

260
00:14:59,870 --> 00:15:01,040
What about Toey?

261
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:04,160
If he finds out, we'll all get scolded.

262
00:15:04,755 --> 00:15:06,360
Everyone else is still working.

263
00:15:07,142 --> 00:15:10,470
Hong, we'll just sneak out. He won't even know.

264
00:15:10,523 --> 00:15:13,124
Come on, we've done it plenty of times.

265
00:15:13,478 --> 00:15:17,400
Exactly. I don't think it's right.

266
00:15:17,640 --> 00:15:19,400
So, are you coming or not?

267
00:15:21,254 --> 00:15:22,255
I'm coming.

268
00:15:23,254 --> 00:15:24,255
- That's more like it!
- There you go!

269
00:15:25,100 --> 00:15:26,262
Let's go, Mutta.

270
00:15:34,587 --> 00:15:37,280
We're just going out for lunch. Why all the sneaking around?

271
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:39,600
Because it's not lunchtime yet, Mutta.

272
00:15:39,600 --> 00:15:41,680
Look, there's hardly anyone around.

273
00:15:45,467 --> 00:15:47,568
Hello, Director.

274
00:15:51,192 --> 00:15:52,193
Where are you all going?

275
00:15:52,800 --> 00:15:55,520
We're going for som tam outside the Ministry. Want to join us?

276
00:15:57,294 --> 00:15:59,160
Why don't you come have lunch with me instead? Let's go.

277
00:16:06,288 --> 00:16:08,240
I'll pretend I didn't notice

278
00:16:08,571 --> 00:16:10,680
that you all took your lunch break early.

279
00:16:12,326 --> 00:16:16,000
You can even come back a little late. I won't mind.

280
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:18,301
But

281
00:16:19,787 --> 00:16:22,720
you mustn't gossip about me and Mutta having lunch together.

282
00:16:23,526 --> 00:16:25,894
Understood?

283
00:16:26,420 --> 00:16:28,800
Yes, Director.

284
00:16:47,040 --> 00:16:52,041
Oshi, Mutta just went out to lunch with the Director.

285
00:16:54,606 --> 00:16:58,240
On the day of the e-bidding, we'll rig it so they win.

286
00:16:59,326 --> 00:17:00,400
But don't worry.

287
00:17:00,510 --> 00:17:03,180
Our system is foolproof. No one will ever catch us.

288
00:17:13,611 --> 00:17:15,012
In my opinion,

289
00:17:15,584 --> 00:17:17,385
this will improve our image among the younger generation.

290
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:19,601
We're giving startups a chance,

291
00:17:20,101 --> 00:17:22,602
which also aligns with our future policies.

292
00:17:32,651 --> 00:17:35,035
Are you sure your wife won't come after me?

293
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:38,700
After what happened, she'll probably be keeping a close eye on you.

294
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:41,701
She's too busy for that.

295
00:17:42,446 --> 00:17:44,880
She's caught up in some massive project of hers.

296
00:17:46,222 --> 00:17:47,640
You mean the smart card project?

297
00:17:50,155 --> 00:17:51,730
You're interested in that sort of thing, Mutta?

298
00:17:52,715 --> 00:17:54,350
I just happened to see it on the news.

299
00:18:01,766 --> 00:18:02,767
Cheers!

300
00:18:10,472 --> 00:18:11,473
Mutta,

301
00:18:12,152 --> 00:18:15,400
do you know that doll called Babina-Babini or something?

302
00:18:16,766 --> 00:18:19,120
- Bambinana?
- Yeah, that's the one!

303
00:18:20,040 --> 00:18:22,360
My daughter really wants one.

304
00:18:22,766 --> 00:18:24,480
But the limited edition is sold out.

305
00:18:24,787 --> 00:18:26,680
It's driving me crazy. I have no idea where to find one.

306
00:18:27,326 --> 00:18:29,600
Do you know where I could buy one?

307
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:33,807
Once a limited edition sells out, that's it.

308
00:18:34,824 --> 00:18:37,300
It could take years before someone resells one.

309
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:39,080
Years?

310
00:18:41,752 --> 00:18:43,520
My daughter threw a tantrum all night.

311
00:18:43,867 --> 00:18:46,700
She said we didn't love her because we couldn't buy her that toy.

312
00:18:48,075 --> 00:18:50,000
Being a parent is tough.

313
00:18:50,342 --> 00:18:52,280
If I could turn back time, I wouldn't have had her.

314
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:59,300
By the way, have you gotten your contraceptive implant yet?

315
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:02,601
Yes, I have.

316
00:19:03,232 --> 00:19:04,233
Really?

317
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:05,901
That's great!

318
00:19:05,947 --> 00:19:09,000
After we finish eating, let's go have some fun.

319
00:19:09,846 --> 00:19:13,360
Ever since you came back, I haven't gotten any action from you.

320
00:19:14,734 --> 00:19:16,700
- Maybe another day.
- No way!

321
00:19:17,843 --> 00:19:19,600
I'm not letting you put me off anymore.

322
00:19:20,800 --> 00:19:22,320
Even if there's a red light,

323
00:19:23,128 --> 00:19:24,160
I'm going straight through it.

324
00:19:25,576 --> 00:19:27,440
I don't care how much the fine is.

325
00:20:09,390 --> 00:20:10,720
Wait, Director.

326
00:20:11,064 --> 00:20:13,320
Let's get a little tipsy first. It'll spice things up.

327
00:20:16,387 --> 00:20:18,880
Sure! I'll make it extra spicy for you.

328
00:20:20,062 --> 00:20:21,063
Bottoms up!

329
00:20:36,702 --> 00:20:38,300
Director! Director!

330
00:20:38,526 --> 00:20:40,727
You're the best, Director!

331
00:20:41,043 --> 00:20:42,560
Director? More like Dynamite in Bed!

332
00:20:42,792 --> 00:20:45,280
Director! Oh, Director!

333
00:20:46,600 --> 00:20:47,601
Director!

334
00:21:00,518 --> 00:21:02,600
Director! Director!

335
00:21:42,088 --> 00:21:43,089
Mutta.

336
00:21:43,822 --> 00:21:44,823
What happened?

337
00:21:46,211 --> 00:21:49,780
You thrust so hard you nearly broke my pelvis,

338
00:21:50,072 --> 00:21:51,360
and now you're asking what happened?

339
00:21:55,110 --> 00:21:56,111
Huh?

340
00:21:56,550 --> 00:21:57,651
Wait, we already had sex?

341
00:21:59,504 --> 00:22:00,560
It's almost four o'clock.

342
00:22:00,752 --> 00:22:03,440
Hurry back to work. It's almost time to clock out.

343
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,881
How the hell is that possible?

344
00:22:42,609 --> 00:22:44,320
Hey, baby. What's up?

345
00:22:44,592 --> 00:22:47,240
Babe, sorry for waking you up in the middle of the night.

346
00:22:47,659 --> 00:22:50,080
I need a huge favor.

347
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:53,300
I want a Bambinana doll with a red hat.

348
00:22:53,500 --> 00:22:55,440
It's only sold at the store in Vegas.

349
00:22:55,501 --> 00:22:58,300
Do you have any friends in Vegas who could get one for me?

350
00:22:58,700 --> 00:22:59,920
Friends in Vegas?

351
00:23:01,800 --> 00:23:04,001
No. Why don't you just buy it online?

352
00:23:04,801 --> 00:23:07,920
It's a limited edition, only available in-store.

353
00:23:08,894 --> 00:23:11,640
How about this, babe? Could you drive there and get one for me?

354
00:23:12,318 --> 00:23:14,760
Sure, I'll take care of it this weekend.

355
00:23:15,550 --> 00:23:17,960
You have to go tonight! It goes on sale at 10 a.m.

356
00:23:18,232 --> 00:23:20,180
And you'll have to line up. There are only a few available.

357
00:23:20,478 --> 00:23:21,520
At three in the morning?

358
00:23:22,355 --> 00:23:23,640
You want me to go buy a toy right now?

359
00:23:24,451 --> 00:23:26,760
If you drive from here to Vegas, you'll get there by morning.

360
00:23:27,064 --> 00:23:28,760
Please, babe?

361
00:23:29,230 --> 00:23:30,231
I'm begging you.

362
00:23:31,827 --> 00:23:33,880
Hmm. I'll take care of it…

363
00:23:34,328 --> 00:23:35,329
as always.

364
00:23:39,400 --> 00:23:41,401
[Bangkok Remand Prison, 125th Anniversary]

365
00:23:53,366 --> 00:23:54,367
Aren't you going to eat?

366
00:23:55,702 --> 00:23:56,903
I'm sick of this dog food.

367
00:23:58,219 --> 00:23:59,840
I'm eating outside today.

368
00:24:00,578 --> 00:24:03,000
Keep talking big. You'll starve to death.

369
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:08,400
- Jintana.
- Yes.

370
00:24:08,440 --> 00:24:09,840
- Jongsawat.
- That's right.

371
00:24:12,272 --> 00:24:16,240
You've been granted a sentence reduction under the Royal Pardon Decree.

372
00:24:16,470 --> 00:24:19,840
Your recalculated sentence ends today.

373
00:24:20,152 --> 00:24:21,153
Prepare for release.

374
00:24:23,422 --> 00:24:24,423
Thank you.

375
00:24:25,784 --> 00:24:26,785
Bye-bye!

376
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:27,901
Bye-bye!

377
00:24:33,179 --> 00:24:36,480
Do you think I've been too hard on Andrew, making him do all this stuff?

378
00:24:38,614 --> 00:24:42,320
A little, yeah. I actually feel sorry for your boyfriend.

379
00:24:42,700 --> 00:24:44,080
Look how he does everything you ask.

380
00:24:44,501 --> 00:24:46,300
But you barely seem to care about him.

381
00:24:46,800 --> 00:24:47,801
Of course I care!

382
00:24:48,432 --> 00:24:51,800
I just want that stupid banana doll to mess with Nopnapha.

383
00:24:52,422 --> 00:24:53,723
I've come up with a new plan.

384
00:24:54,406 --> 00:24:56,080
I'm going to use her daughter against her.

385
00:24:56,704 --> 00:24:59,259
What? You're dragging a child into this too?

386
00:24:59,931 --> 00:25:01,286
What are you planning to do to the poor girl?

387
00:25:07,648 --> 00:25:10,206
Hang on. It's my condo management calling.

388
00:25:13,110 --> 00:25:14,111
Hello?

389
00:25:16,100 --> 00:25:17,101
What?

390
00:25:18,701 --> 00:25:19,902
Are you sure there's no mistake?

391
00:25:21,600 --> 00:25:22,601
Okay, I'll come down.

392
00:25:23,900 --> 00:25:24,901
I've got to go. Talk later.

393
00:25:36,275 --> 00:25:38,200
Mutta! Mutta!

394
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:40,360
Is that you, sweetheart? Mutta!

395
00:25:40,870 --> 00:25:43,240
I've missed you so much, my dear.

396
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:50,640
Sorry, ma'am. You've got the wrong person.

397
00:25:51,320 --> 00:25:53,860
You bitch! Why didn't you say so sooner?

398
00:26:02,558 --> 00:26:04,520
Ugh, so annoying!

399
00:26:06,264 --> 00:26:09,800
What the hell are you crying for? What the hell?

400
00:26:10,856 --> 00:26:12,600
You're such a damn nuisance!

401
00:26:13,128 --> 00:26:14,440
Why are you crying?

402
00:26:15,848 --> 00:26:18,080
Look at me! I said stop!

403
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,800
I said stop!

404
00:26:20,296 --> 00:26:22,080
I told you to stop! Why won't you stop, huh?

405
00:26:22,120 --> 00:26:24,160
Why won't you stop? Stop it already!

406
00:26:25,214 --> 00:26:26,680
Stop hitting your children, Jintana!

407
00:26:28,606 --> 00:26:31,080
You're under arrest for robbery and murder.

408
00:26:31,576 --> 00:26:32,867
You'll have to come with us for questioning.

409
00:26:32,968 --> 00:26:35,080
- Let's go!
- I didn't do it! Don't arrest me!

410
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:37,720
I was just trying to make money to feed my kids!

411
00:26:37,984 --> 00:26:39,800
I was just trying to provide for my kids!

412
00:26:39,897 --> 00:26:40,898
Take her to the police station.

413
00:26:47,898 --> 00:26:48,899
Mutta!

414
00:26:49,800 --> 00:26:50,801
Is that you, Mutta?

415
00:26:53,900 --> 00:26:54,901
It's Mom.

416
00:26:55,501 --> 00:26:58,440
You remember me, don't you, sweetheart? Don't you?

417
00:27:04,891 --> 00:27:06,250
This place is huge!

418
00:27:10,184 --> 00:27:11,930
How much did it cost? Ten million?

419
00:27:13,100 --> 00:27:14,920
I didn't buy it. I'm renting.

420
00:27:16,600 --> 00:27:18,501
I knew it!

421
00:27:18,570 --> 00:27:21,501
How could a lowly civil servant ever get rich?

422
00:27:23,166 --> 00:27:24,680
Why don't you try selling yourself?

423
00:27:24,700 --> 00:27:26,801
Put your youth and beauty to good use.

424
00:27:30,598 --> 00:27:31,728
Oh, and what about that bitch Munin?

425
00:27:32,096 --> 00:27:33,097
Where is she?

426
00:27:33,216 --> 00:27:34,360
I heard some foreigner adopted her

427
00:27:35,200 --> 00:27:37,920
from the foster home, right?

428
00:27:39,080 --> 00:27:40,081
Yeah.

429
00:27:40,440 --> 00:27:42,000
That bitch sure got lucky.

430
00:27:42,771 --> 00:27:45,200
I bet that foreigner took her as a wife.

431
00:27:46,830 --> 00:27:48,600
Has she ever contacted you?

432
00:27:51,500 --> 00:27:53,100
- No.
- What an ungrateful bitch!

433
00:27:53,664 --> 00:27:55,920
She made it big and forgot all about her own sister.

434
00:27:57,201 --> 00:28:00,120
Forget about her, Mom. Just tell me why you're here.

435
00:28:00,750 --> 00:28:01,751
Why are you here?

436
00:28:03,542 --> 00:28:07,080
Does a mother need a reason to visit her own daughter?

437
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:09,126
I missed you!

438
00:28:09,318 --> 00:28:10,880
Didn't you miss me at all?

439
00:28:11,771 --> 00:28:13,880
It's been over twenty years since we last saw each other.

440
00:28:16,696 --> 00:28:17,697
I...

441
00:28:18,664 --> 00:28:20,600
I never thought I'd see you again.

442
00:28:20,872 --> 00:28:22,340
They told me you were sentenced to life in prison.

443
00:28:23,443 --> 00:28:27,200
Nobody stays in prison for life. Everyone gets their sentence reduced.

444
00:28:29,544 --> 00:28:33,640
But while I was in prison, I missed you two so much.

445
00:28:34,488 --> 00:28:37,760
I counted down the days until I could see my daughters again.

446
00:28:38,787 --> 00:28:40,979
Mom, just get to the point.

447
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,001
What do you want?

448
00:28:46,700 --> 00:28:48,400
Do you have some money you could give me?

449
00:28:48,742 --> 00:28:51,100
I want to use it to start a new life with my boyfriend.

450
00:28:55,043 --> 00:28:57,640
Forty-eight... forty-nine... fifty.

451
00:28:59,619 --> 00:29:02,686
That's my girl. I raised you right.

452
00:29:03,038 --> 00:29:04,766
I'll use this money to buy a phone.

453
00:29:04,840 --> 00:29:08,241
Then we can call each other whenever we miss each other.

454
00:29:08,700 --> 00:29:09,701
There's no need.

455
00:29:10,000 --> 00:29:11,801
Go start a new family with your boyfriend, Mom.

456
00:29:11,998 --> 00:29:13,520
And let's stay out of each other's lives.

457
00:29:14,899 --> 00:29:16,320
How can you be so heartless?

458
00:29:18,369 --> 00:29:21,072
A mother and daughter can never truly cut ties.

459
00:29:22,100 --> 00:29:23,101
But...

460
00:29:23,574 --> 00:29:26,880
if you give me a monthly allowance,

461
00:29:26,890 --> 00:29:29,160
I might not miss you quite so much.

462
00:29:35,656 --> 00:29:37,320
Is this the car you called to pick me up?

463
00:29:39,100 --> 00:29:42,360
How fancy! I haven't ridden in an air-conditioned car in ages.

464
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:46,401
Well, I'll be off now, Munin.

465
00:29:47,901 --> 00:29:48,902
Mutta.

466
00:29:49,736 --> 00:29:51,300
- Are you Mutta or Munin?
- Just go, Mom.

467
00:30:24,480 --> 00:30:26,806
So, did you get it?

468
00:30:27,643 --> 00:30:28,980
Yeah, I got it.

469
00:30:32,251 --> 00:30:33,252
Thanks.

470
00:30:33,547 --> 00:30:35,131
Thank you so much. Love you.

471
00:30:39,843 --> 00:30:40,844
Hey!

472
00:30:41,347 --> 00:30:42,348
What happened?

473
00:30:42,654 --> 00:30:45,347
I got the toy for you, right?

474
00:30:45,655 --> 00:30:48,600
I was about to mail it, but then...

475
00:30:50,326 --> 00:30:51,327
as you can see.

476
00:30:54,038 --> 00:30:56,576
What did the doctor say? Is it serious?

477
00:30:57,360 --> 00:30:59,680
Just a broken leg. I'll be in a cast for two months.

478
00:31:03,147 --> 00:31:04,360
I'm sorry.

479
00:31:05,755 --> 00:31:07,880
I don't even know what to say, except...

480
00:31:09,339 --> 00:31:11,840
sorry and get well soon.

481
00:31:15,040 --> 00:31:16,440
Have you sent me the package yet?

482
00:31:20,341 --> 00:31:21,342
What?

483
00:31:21,694 --> 00:31:23,800
Your mom got out of prison and showed up at your place asking for money.

484
00:31:24,350 --> 00:31:27,240
And your boyfriend Andrew broke his leg in a car accident.

485
00:31:27,662 --> 00:31:31,160
Seriously, your life is one disaster after another.

486
00:31:31,200 --> 00:31:32,646
How does everything get so chaotic?

487
00:31:33,414 --> 00:31:34,640
I guess I'm just having a run of bad luck.

488
00:31:36,651 --> 00:31:38,950
I hope nothing else happens to give me a heart attack.

489
00:31:46,091 --> 00:31:47,120
What's wrong, Khwan?

490
00:31:47,750 --> 00:31:49,880
The smart card project e-bidding results are out.

491
00:31:50,560 --> 00:31:51,961
Wait! Don't open it yet!

492
00:31:52,539 --> 00:31:53,540
I need to brace myself.

493
00:31:56,624 --> 00:31:57,625
Okay, open it.

494
00:32:01,696 --> 00:32:05,800
We regret to inform you that your company was not selected.

495
00:32:06,032 --> 00:32:08,678
Thank you for your interest in participating in the bidding process.

496
00:32:08,790 --> 00:32:12,360
We hope you'll participate in our future projects.

497
00:32:21,966 --> 00:32:24,650
Looks like we're both having a run of bad luck lately.

498
00:32:26,167 --> 00:32:28,568
It's okay. We can wait for the next project.

499
00:32:29,347 --> 00:32:30,840
I'm not upset about losing the contract.

500
00:32:31,734 --> 00:32:33,920
I'm upset that I missed my chance to get revenge on that bitch Nopnapha.

501
00:32:40,535 --> 00:32:41,536
Hey,

502
00:32:42,246 --> 00:32:45,051
can we find out which company won the bid?

503
00:32:58,800 --> 00:32:59,801
Wow.

504
00:33:00,500 --> 00:33:03,360
Your credentials are seriously impressive.

505
00:33:05,142 --> 00:33:07,143
It's such a shame, though.

506
00:33:08,374 --> 00:33:10,575
My company isn't hiring anyone right now.

507
00:33:13,635 --> 00:33:17,560
I saw that your company won the smart card project bid.

508
00:33:18,243 --> 00:33:20,400
So I'd love to put my experience to good use

509
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:22,480
and help develop our country.

510
00:33:24,081 --> 00:33:25,600
I'd even be willing to work without pay.

511
00:33:28,082 --> 00:33:29,083
Please?

512
00:33:30,712 --> 00:33:32,300
Just give me a chance to work with you.

513
00:33:38,928 --> 00:33:40,840
I'll arrange a private office for you.

514
00:33:42,176 --> 00:33:44,043
That way, I can train you...

515
00:33:45,371 --> 00:33:46,372
without any interruptions.

516
00:33:47,867 --> 00:33:48,868
First things first,

517
00:33:49,942 --> 00:33:51,640
we need to turn on the computer.

518
00:33:53,382 --> 00:33:56,820
I'd like to start by reviewing all the company's information.

519
00:33:57,915 --> 00:33:59,016
We can discuss everything else later.

520
00:34:16,500 --> 00:34:17,501
Call me when you're done.

521
00:34:59,811 --> 00:35:01,360
Isn't Mutta joining us for lunch today?

522
00:35:03,422 --> 00:35:05,320
She called in sick today.

523
00:35:05,811 --> 00:35:09,080
I'm worried about her. I hope it's nothing serious.

524
00:35:12,500 --> 00:35:14,901
- Mind if I join you?
- Of course, Veekit! Have a seat.

525
00:35:26,798 --> 00:35:27,799
Hello?

526
00:35:27,832 --> 00:35:30,160
Are you sick, Mutta? Is it serious?

527
00:35:32,600 --> 00:35:34,201
I've got a sore throat and a fever.

528
00:35:34,700 --> 00:35:36,780
I've already taken some medicine. I should be back at work tomorrow.

529
00:35:37,478 --> 00:35:40,160
Have you had lunch yet? Want me to bring you something?

530
00:35:40,654 --> 00:35:42,960
No, I've already ordered food to my condo.

531
00:35:43,571 --> 00:35:44,572
Thanks, though.

532
00:35:44,910 --> 00:35:45,911
Munin.

533
00:35:47,592 --> 00:35:48,700
Let's go have lunch.

534
00:35:50,520 --> 00:35:51,760
I'd like to treat you to a welcome lunch.

535
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:55,001
I've got to go. Talk later.

536
00:35:55,854 --> 00:35:57,000
Hello? Mutta? Wait!

537
00:36:00,643 --> 00:36:01,644
Who the hell is Munin?

538
00:36:04,899 --> 00:36:05,900
- Whiskey?
- Yes?

539
00:36:06,131 --> 00:36:09,032
Do you know who Mutta lives with at her condo?

540
00:36:10,595 --> 00:36:12,300
As far as I know, she lives alone.

541
00:36:12,376 --> 00:36:14,120
Why do you ask, Veekit? Is something wrong?

542
00:36:17,377 --> 00:36:18,578
No, it's nothing.

543
00:36:18,942 --> 00:36:22,200
I'm just worried there's no one to take care of her.

544
00:36:22,220 --> 00:36:23,760
Oh, I see.

545
00:36:26,283 --> 00:36:29,320
Do either of you know someone named Munin?

546
00:36:29,952 --> 00:36:30,953
Munin?

547
00:36:31,563 --> 00:36:34,440
Who's Munin? Mutta's never mentioned that name.

548
00:36:35,317 --> 00:36:36,318
Hong?

549
00:36:37,400 --> 00:36:38,700
Do you know who Munin is?

550
00:36:45,366 --> 00:36:46,367
Mun...

551
00:36:47,280 --> 00:36:48,281
Ta...

552
00:36:50,281 --> 00:36:53,082
I know gossiping is wrong.

553
00:36:54,910 --> 00:36:55,911
Hong.

554
00:36:56,911 --> 00:36:58,240
Save your mouth for eating.

555
00:37:01,459 --> 00:37:02,760
I am eating.

556
00:37:06,115 --> 00:37:07,300
And it's delicious.

557
00:37:12,208 --> 00:37:13,840
- Could we ask you a few questions?
- Ma'am!

558
00:37:14,336 --> 00:37:17,700
Regarding the Tax Department Director-General's corruption scandal
involving three billion baht,

559
00:37:17,744 --> 00:37:19,345
what progress has been made, ma'am?

560
00:37:19,700 --> 00:37:22,000
Our investigation has uncovered some facts.

561
00:37:22,040 --> 00:37:24,160
I'm taking steps to pursue legal action.

562
00:37:24,219 --> 00:37:26,440
Some say the Director-General might get away with it.

563
00:37:26,528 --> 00:37:28,040
Because he's one of your people, Nopnapha.

564
00:37:28,342 --> 00:37:29,776
What do you have to say about that?

565
00:37:30,278 --> 00:37:33,080
Anyone who says that clearly doesn't know me well enough.

566
00:37:34,689 --> 00:37:36,320
Throughout my political career,

567
00:37:36,952 --> 00:37:39,760
I've always upheld honesty and integrity. Everyone knows that.

568
00:37:41,700 --> 00:37:42,880
I don't want to hear such accusations again.

569
00:37:47,500 --> 00:37:51,520
Ma'am, someone sent us information about Hype Tech, the company
that won the smart card project.

570
00:37:51,600 --> 00:37:53,640
They have a history of colluding to rig government bids.

571
00:37:53,701 --> 00:37:54,702
What?

572
00:37:54,875 --> 00:37:55,876
Who sent it?

573
00:37:56,198 --> 00:37:57,920
It was sent anonymously, with no source identified.

574
00:37:59,115 --> 00:38:00,480
Then double-check the information for me.

575
00:38:00,700 --> 00:38:04,300
If it's true, award the contract to the second-place bidder instead.

576
00:38:05,100 --> 00:38:08,301
There have been too many corruption scandals lately. We can't afford another one.

577
00:38:35,118 --> 00:38:36,119
Babe!

578
00:38:37,062 --> 00:38:39,440
Thank you so much. I really love you.

579
00:38:41,563 --> 00:38:43,080
I love you but…

580
00:38:44,672 --> 00:38:46,200
I've been feeling unhappy for a while.

581
00:38:47,787 --> 00:38:50,600
What's wrong? What's the matter?

582
00:38:51,046 --> 00:38:54,120
I care about you, Nina. I really do. It's just…

583
00:38:55,443 --> 00:38:57,400
I don't think our relationship is healthy anymore.

584
00:38:57,837 --> 00:38:58,838
Calm down.

585
00:38:59,406 --> 00:39:01,080
We can talk this through.

586
00:39:01,598 --> 00:39:04,480
I've just been a little busy lately.

587
00:39:04,515 --> 00:39:07,300
- But…
- Honey, your coffee is getting cold.

588
00:39:07,916 --> 00:39:08,917
I'm coming.

589
00:39:13,160 --> 00:39:14,440
This is what I tried to tell you.

590
00:39:15,161 --> 00:39:16,162
Goodbye, Nina.

591
00:39:32,500 --> 00:39:33,501
[Jolene]

592
00:39:35,611 --> 00:39:38,760
Jolene, you won't believe what just happened to me.

593
00:39:39,430 --> 00:39:41,800
Hold on, Munin. Listen carefully.

594
00:39:41,872 --> 00:39:42,960
You're not going to believe this.

595
00:39:43,243 --> 00:39:46,170
Nopnapha called me in to sign the smart card project contract.

596
00:39:46,379 --> 00:39:47,820
Your plan worked.

597
00:39:47,840 --> 00:39:51,341
That company got kicked out, and we got the contract instead.

598
00:39:51,471 --> 00:39:55,120
We're about to take on a nationwide project.

599
00:39:57,216 --> 00:39:58,600
I've got to go.

600
00:40:21,024 --> 00:40:22,600
Drinks are on me tonight.

601
00:40:46,240 --> 00:40:48,241
[Veekit]

602
00:41:05,070 --> 00:41:06,071
Mutta.

603
00:41:06,275 --> 00:41:09,320
I brought you some rice porridge, congee, and fruit.

604
00:41:11,542 --> 00:41:12,543
Thank you.

605
00:41:13,830 --> 00:41:14,831
Still not feeling any better?

606
00:41:15,300 --> 00:41:16,880
Do you need any medicine? I can go get some.

607
00:41:17,611 --> 00:41:19,640
It's okay. I'm just feeling a little weak.

608
00:41:23,500 --> 00:41:24,501
Well, then...

609
00:41:25,301 --> 00:41:27,002
Make sure you eat, take your medicine, and get plenty of rest.

610
00:41:27,702 --> 00:41:30,100
And if you're still sick tomorrow, don't force yourself to go to work, okay?

611
00:41:35,976 --> 00:41:36,977
I'll get going, then.

612
00:41:40,357 --> 00:41:41,358
Veekit.

613
00:41:46,128 --> 00:41:47,376
Could you stay and keep me company for a while?

614
00:41:54,475 --> 00:41:55,476
Mutta.

615
00:41:59,027 --> 00:42:00,028
Mutta.

616
00:42:04,046 --> 00:42:05,047
Mutta.

617
00:42:07,247 --> 00:42:08,248
Why do you keep calling my name?

618
00:42:12,248 --> 00:42:13,249
Thank you.

619
00:42:19,008 --> 00:42:22,211
You know, I just realized I'd probably get stuck in traffic if I left now.

620
00:42:23,907 --> 00:42:24,908
Hey.

621
00:42:25,944 --> 00:42:27,445
Can you sit and talk with me for a bit?

622
00:42:38,118 --> 00:42:40,160
You can choose between rice soup and congee.

623
00:42:40,715 --> 00:42:42,520
Or we can split them both.

624
00:42:44,998 --> 00:42:46,600
I'll have the rice soup. You can have the congee.

625
00:42:50,032 --> 00:42:51,033
You said it!

626
00:42:59,694 --> 00:43:02,180
- How is it? Good?
- Yeah.

627
00:43:14,187 --> 00:43:16,272
Wow, you must've been starving.

628
00:43:16,678 --> 00:43:18,400
Did you buy this for me or for yourself?

629
00:43:19,974 --> 00:43:21,120
For myself, obviously.

630
00:43:26,245 --> 00:43:27,246
I bought it for you.

631
00:43:28,702 --> 00:43:29,703
Really!

632
00:43:31,731 --> 00:43:33,760
I thought alpacas only ate grass and vegetables.

633
00:43:33,923 --> 00:43:35,040
But you eat everything, huh?

634
00:43:36,766 --> 00:43:40,120
Who says? There's pork in here too. See?

635
00:43:41,558 --> 00:43:42,800
Here, I'll eat this, too.

636
00:43:44,443 --> 00:43:46,000
Here, have some fruit.

637
00:43:51,259 --> 00:43:52,440
Now that's more like an alpaca.

638
00:43:53,670 --> 00:43:54,671
It's good, isn't it?

639
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:56,761
It's okay.

640
00:43:58,240 --> 00:43:59,241
Just making sure it's not too hot.

641
00:44:12,840 --> 00:44:15,841
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

642
00:44:16,430 --> 00:44:19,300
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

643
00:44:22,027 --> 00:44:24,080
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday...♪

644
00:44:25,118 --> 00:44:28,870
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

645
00:44:37,400 --> 00:44:40,600
For your birthday this year, Daddy wishes you'll be a good girl,

646
00:44:40,816 --> 00:44:42,817
do well in school,

647
00:44:42,880 --> 00:44:45,881
and stop throwing tantrums.

648
00:44:46,128 --> 00:44:49,640
You're growing into a young lady. Keep this up, and all the boys will run away.

649
00:44:53,046 --> 00:44:56,800
Okay, my birthday wish for you, Titus, is that you'll listen to me and behave.

650
00:44:56,847 --> 00:44:58,840
And whenever you go somewhere, tell me first.

651
00:44:59,520 --> 00:45:01,040
Don't scare me like that again.

652
00:45:01,211 --> 00:45:02,320
And one more thing.

653
00:45:03,918 --> 00:45:06,120
No more screaming, okay?

654
00:45:06,622 --> 00:45:07,623
Okay!

655
00:45:08,120 --> 00:45:09,121
Good girl!

656
00:45:13,832 --> 00:45:15,040
Oh! The pretty sister is here!

657
00:45:15,574 --> 00:45:16,920
- See?
- We just talked about this.

658
00:45:24,510 --> 00:45:25,511
Hey!

659
00:45:37,062 --> 00:45:38,063
Shit!

660
00:45:50,784 --> 00:45:54,120
If I really became your mom, which mom would you love more?

661
00:45:54,251 --> 00:45:57,121
Mom Nopnapha or Mom Mutta?

662
00:45:57,350 --> 00:45:59,320
I'd love Mom Mutta more, of course!

663
00:45:59,595 --> 00:46:01,960
And I'd quit being Mom Nopnapha's daughter, too!

664
00:46:02,043 --> 00:46:05,144
You should be happy that I get along with your daughter, Director.

665
00:46:05,414 --> 00:46:08,615
After all, I'm going to be her mother someday.

666
00:46:12,464 --> 00:46:14,480
When you watch other magicians perform,

667
00:46:14,998 --> 00:46:16,360
can you ever figure out their tricks?

668
00:46:16,412 --> 00:46:18,250
It's not just magicians I can see through.

669
00:46:18,475 --> 00:46:19,840
I can spot liars, too.

670
00:46:20,720 --> 00:46:23,320
So, to you, am I a magician

671
00:46:24,182 --> 00:46:25,183
or a liar?

672
00:46:29,243 --> 00:46:31,644
You filthy tramp! You cheap whore!

673
00:46:31,686 --> 00:46:33,140
Get the hell out of my house! Now!

674
00:46:33,270 --> 00:46:36,040
The reason he doesn't want to come home after work is that

675
00:46:36,297 --> 00:46:37,480
seeing your face is like seeing a ghost!

676
00:46:37,611 --> 00:46:39,680
You're the one who needs to get out!

677
00:46:40,780 --> 00:46:41,781
Come here!

678
00:46:41,814 --> 00:46:43,440
Die, you evil bitch!
